YANI: "Tool" of remove curse.

Weighs 15-20, relative probability 15, cost 50.

Charged in same manner as magical instrument, i.e.

  Created with 4 to 8 charges. Blessed scrolls of charging add 2 to 8
  charges; uncursed scrolls 1 to 4 charges.  Foos cannot have more than
  20 charges.

When applied, uses 1 charge and:

BLESSED: acts as blessed scroll of remove curse

UNCURSED: acts as uncursed scroll of remove curse

CURSED: uncurses itself

Primary purpose: a means of uncursing when wielding a cursed two-handed 
weapon that cannot be destroyed by the RNG, or be rendered useless by 
cursing. Carrying one of these in main inventory with 2+ charges allows 
a player to use a two-hander in safety, ableit requiring up to two moves 
to uncurse. An alternative is to have an artifact two-hander, e.g. )ToM, 
to uncurse itself by #invoking.

Any ideas for a name? There must be many objects reputed to ward off 
curses.


